<h2>9. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS</h2>

<h3>9.1 Performance</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>Req ID</th><th>Requirement</th><th>Target</th></tr>
<tr><td>NF-001</td><td>API response — list queries</td><td>< 2 seconds</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-002</td><td>API response — single record fetch</td><td>< 500 ms</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-003</td><td>PDF report generation</td><td>< 5 seconds</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-004</td><td>Dashboard KPI load time</td><td>< 3 seconds</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-005</td><td>Concurrent user support without degradation</td><td>50 users</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-006</td><td>Database query response time</td><td>< 1 second</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>9.2 Availability & Reliability</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>Req ID</th><th>Requirement</th><th>Target</th></tr>
<tr><td>NF-007</td><td>Uptime during business hours (8 AM - 10 PM)</td><td>99.5%</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-008</td><td>Scheduled maintenance window</td><td>Off-hours only</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-009</td><td>Data backup frequency</td><td>Daily full + hourly incremental</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-010</td><td>Recovery Time Objective (RTO)</td><td>< 4 hours</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-011</td><td>Recovery Point Objective (RPO)</td><td>< 1 hour</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>9.3 Scalability</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>Req ID</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>
<tr><td>NF-012</td><td>Architecture must support future horizontal scaling</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-013</td><td>Modular design allows new modules without core changes</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-014</td><td>DB must efficiently handle 5 years of transactional data</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>9.4 Usability</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>Req ID</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>
<tr><td>NF-015</td><td>Fully responsive: desktop (1920px), laptop (1366px), tablet (768px), mobile (375px)</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-016</td><td>All forms provide real-time validation feedback</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-017</td><td>All data tables support search, sort, filter, and pagination</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-018</td><td>Operable without browser plugins or special software</td></tr>
<tr><td>NF-019</td><td>English UI (Bengali language support in future phase)</td></tr>
</table>

<hr/>

<h2>10. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE REQUIREMENTS</h2>

<table>
<tr><th>Req ID</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>
<tr><td>AR-001</td><td>Backend must follow Modular Monolithic architecture pattern</td></tr>
<tr><td>AR-002</td><td>CQRS implemented via MediatR 12</td></tr>
<tr><td>AR-003</td><td>Each module must have Domain, Application, Infrastructure layers</td></tr>
<tr><td>AR-004</td><td>Modules must not directly reference each other's internal classes</td></tr>
<tr><td>AR-005</td><td>Cross-module communication via published interfaces only</td></tr>
<tr><td>AR-006</td><td>Repository pattern used for all data access</td></tr>
<tr><td>AR-007</td><td>API follows RESTful conventions with versioning (/api/v1/)</td></tr>
<tr><td>AR-008</td><td>All API responses use standard envelope (success, data, message)</td></tr>
</table>

<hr/>

<h2>11. TECHNOLOGY STACK REQUIREMENTS</h2>

<table>
<tr><th>Layer</th><th>Required Technology</th></tr>
<tr><td>Backend Framework</td><td>ASP.NET Core 10 Web API</td></tr>
<tr><td>Architecture Pattern</td><td>Modular Monolithic + CQRS</td></tr>
<tr><td>CQRS Mediator</td><td>MediatR 12+</td></tr>
<tr><td>ORM</td><td>Entity Framework Core 10</td></tr>
<tr><td>Validation</td><td>FluentValidation</td></tr>
<tr><td>Object Mapping</td><td>AutoMapper or Mapster</td></tr>
<tr><td>Logging</td><td>Serilog with Seq sink</td></tr>
<tr><td>Authentication</td><td>ASP.NET Core Identity + JWT Bearer</td></tr>
<tr><td>PDF Reports</td><td>QuestPDF (mandatory, no substitution)</td></tr>
<tr><td>API Documentation</td><td>Swagger / Scalar</td></tr>
<tr><td>Frontend Framework</td><td>Next.js 14 (App Router)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Frontend Language</td><td>TypeScript</td></tr>
<tr><td>UI Components</td><td>shadcn/ui + Radix UI</td></tr>
<tr><td>CSS</td><td>Tailwind CSS</td></tr>
<tr><td>State Management</td><td>Zustand</td></tr>
<tr><td>API Client</td><td>TanStack Query (React Query)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Form Handling</td><td>React Hook Form + Zod</td></tr>
<tr><td>Charts/Graphs</td><td>Recharts or Chart.js</td></tr>
<tr><td>Database</td><td>Microsoft SQL Server 2022</td></tr>
<tr><td>DB Migrations</td><td>EF Core Code-First Migrations</td></tr>
<tr><td>Unit Testing</td><td>xUnit + Moq + FluentAssertions</td></tr>
</table>

<hr/>

<h2>12. DATABASE REQUIREMENTS</h2>

<table>
<tr><th>Req ID</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>
<tr><td>DB-001</td><td>Database engine: Microsoft SQL Server 2022</td></tr>
<tr><td>DB-002</td><td>All primary keys must be GUID (uniqueidentifier)</td></tr>
<tr><td>DB-003</td><td>All critical tables must have soft-delete columns (IsDeleted, DeletedAt, DeletedBy)</td></tr>
<tr><td>DB-004</td><td>All tables must have audit columns (CreatedAt, CreatedBy, UpdatedAt, UpdatedBy)</td></tr>
<tr><td>DB-005</td><td>Schema-per-module strategy: auth, inventory, procurement, production, hr, finance</td></tr>
<tr><td>DB-006</td><td>All money columns: DECIMAL(18,4)</td></tr>
<tr><td>DB-007</td><td>All date columns: DATETIME2(7)</td></tr>
<tr><td>DB-008</td><td>Daily database backup must be automated</td></tr>
<tr><td>DB-009</td><td>Database connections must use connection pooling</td></tr>
<tr><td>DB-010</td><td>All FK columns and filter columns must be indexed</td></tr>
</table>

<hr/>

<h2>13. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS</h2>

<table>
<tr><th>Req ID</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>
<tr><td>SE-001</td><td>All endpoints except login require valid JWT</td></tr>
<tr><td>SE-002</td><td>JWT access tokens expire after 15 minutes</td></tr>
<tr><td>SE-003</td><td>Refresh tokens expire after 7 days (single-use)</td></tr>
<tr><td>SE-004</td><td>Passwords hashed using BCrypt via ASP.NET Identity</td></tr>
<tr><td>SE-005</td><td>All API inputs validated server-side via FluentValidation</td></tr>
<tr><td>SE-006</td><td>SQL injection prevented via parameterized EF Core queries</td></tr>
<tr><td>SE-007</td><td>XSS protection on all user-input fields</td></tr>
<tr><td>SE-008</td><td>CORS configured for trusted frontend origins only</td></tr>
<tr><td>SE-009</td><td>All communication over HTTPS with TLS 1.2 minimum</td></tr>
<tr><td>SE-010</td><td>Sensitive data never logged (passwords, tokens, PII)</td></tr>
<tr><td>SE-011</td><td>Account lockout after 5 consecutive failed login attempts</td></tr>
<tr><td>SE-012</td><td>All permission checks enforced server-side</td></tr>
<tr><td>SE-013</td><td>API rate limiting to prevent abuse</td></tr>
</table>

<hr/>

<h2>14. UI/UX REQUIREMENTS</h2>

<table>
<tr><th>Req ID</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>
<tr><td>UX-001</td><td>Fully responsive: desktop, tablet, mobile</td></tr>
<tr><td>UX-002</td><td>Sidebar navigation dynamically renders based on user permissions</td></tr>
<tr><td>UX-003</td><td>All data lists: search, server-side filter/sort/paginate</td></tr>
<tr><td>UX-004</td><td>Forms show real-time validation errors</td></tr>
<tr><td>UX-005</td><td>Confirmation dialogs before all destructive operations</td></tr>
<tr><td>UX-006</td><td>Loading spinners during all async operations</td></tr>
<tr><td>UX-007</td><td>Success and error toast notifications after all actions</td></tr>
<tr><td>UX-008</td><td>Application supports light and dark mode</td></tr>
<tr><td>UX-009</td><td>All interactive elements have unique, descriptive IDs</td></tr>
<tr><td>UX-010</td><td>Page load time under 3 seconds on standard broadband</td></tr>
</table>

<hr/>

<h2>15. INTEGRATION REQUIREMENTS</h2>

<table>
<tr><th>Integration</th><th>Type</th><th>Priority</th><th>Phase</th></tr>
<tr><td>Biometric attendance system</td><td>CSV import</td><td>High</td><td>V1</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bank payment file export</td><td>CSV export</td><td>High</td><td>V1</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMTP email server</td><td>Outbound only</td><td>Medium</td><td>V1</td></tr>
<tr><td>Future: SMS Gateway</td><td>Outbound</td><td>Low</td><td>V2</td></tr>
<tr><td>Future: ERP system integration</td><td>REST API</td><td>Low</td><td>V3</td></tr>
</table>

<hr/>

<h2>16. REPORT & DOCUMENT REQUIREMENTS</h2>

<table>
<tr><th>Requirement</th></tr>
<tr><td>All PDF reports generated using QuestPDF library (mandatory)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Report header: company logo, name, address, report title</td></tr>
<tr><td>Report footer: page number (X of Y), generation date/time</td></tr>
<tr><td>Reports support A4 and Letter paper size (configurable per report)</td></tr>
<tr><td>All report endpoints require Export permission</td></tr>
<tr><td>Reports downloadable as binary PDF streams</td></tr>
<tr><td>Report generation logged in audit trail</td></tr>
<tr><td>All reports rendered server-side (no client-side PDF generation)</td></tr>
</table>

<hr/>

<h2>17. PERFORMANCE REQUIREMENTS</h2>

<table>
<tr><th>Metric</th><th>Requirement</th></tr>
<tr><td>Max concurrent users</td><td>50 (v1), scalable to 200 (future)</td></tr>
<tr><td>API list query response</td><td>< 2 seconds (10,000+ records)</td></tr>
<tr><td>API single record response</td><td>< 500 milliseconds</td></tr>
<tr><td>PDF report generation</td><td>< 5 seconds</td></tr>
<tr><td>Page initial load (Next.js)</td><td>< 3 seconds</td></tr>
<tr><td>Database query execution</td><td>< 1 second for standard queries</td></tr>
<tr><td>File upload size limit</td><td>10 MB per file</td></tr>
</table>

<hr/>

<h2>18. DEPLOYMENT REQUIREMENTS</h2>

<table>
<tr><th>Requirement</th></tr>
<tr><td>Backend deployable on Windows Server with IIS</td></tr>
<tr><td>Docker containerization support (optional for future use)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Frontend deployable as Next.js standalone build</td></tr>
<tr><td>Environment-based configuration: Development, Staging, Production</td></tr>
<tr><td>Database migrations run automatically on deployment</td></tr>
<tr><td>Swagger/Scalar API docs available in Dev/Staging only (disabled in Production)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Application must enforce SSL/HTTPS in production</td></tr>
<tr><td>CI/CD pipeline recommended (GitHub Actions or Azure DevOps)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Environment variables used for all secrets (no hardcoded credentials)</td></tr>
</table>

<hr/>

<h2>19. GLOSSARY OF TERMS</h2>

<table>
<tr><th>Term</th><th>Definition</th></tr>
<tr><td>AQL</td><td>Acceptance Quality Limit — standard for sampling in QC inspection</td></tr>
<tr><td>BOM</td><td>Bill of Materials — list of materials required per style/product</td></tr>
<tr><td>CQRS</td><td>Command Query Responsibility Segregation — architecture pattern</td></tr>
<tr><td>GRN</td><td>Goods Received Note — document recording received materials from supplier</td></tr>
<tr><td>JWT</td><td>JSON Web Token — stateless authentication token</td></tr>
<tr><td>KPI</td><td>Key Performance Indicator — measurable business metric</td></tr>
<tr><td>LC</td><td>Letter of Credit — payment instrument for export orders</td></tr>
<tr><td>MediatR</td><td>.NET library implementing the Mediator pattern for CQRS</td></tr>
<tr><td>PO</td><td>Purchase Order — formal order to a supplier</td></tr>
<tr><td>QC</td><td>Quality Control — process of ensuring product meets standards</td></tr>
<tr><td>UAT</td><td>User Acceptance Testing — final testing by business users</td></tr>
<tr><td>WIP</td><td>Work-in-Progress — items in mid-production stage</td></tr>
<tr><td>FIFO</td><td>First In, First Out — inventory valuation method</td></tr>
<tr><td>COA</td><td>Chart of Accounts — structured list of all accounting accounts</td></tr>
<tr><td>ERP</td><td>Enterprise Resource Planning — integrated business management system</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMTP</td><td>Simple Mail Transfer Protocol — email sending protocol</td></tr>
<tr><td>REST</td><td>Representational State Transfer — API architectural style</td></tr>
<tr><td>ORM</td><td>Object-Relational Mapper — database abstraction layer</td></tr>
<tr><td>CRUD</td><td>Create, Read, Update, Delete — basic data operations</td></tr>
<tr><td>RTO</td><td>Recovery Time Objective — max acceptable downtime</td></tr>
<tr><td>RPO</td><td>Recovery Point Objective — max acceptable data loss window</td></tr>
</table>

